                <pb facs="0554" n="480" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg480"/>

                <head>No. 10.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#center">[Telegram.—<date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1865-02-04">February 4, 1865</date>—5 p. m.]</dateline></opener>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Official.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">To the Consular Agent of the United States at
                        Ferrol:</hi></p>
                <p>Protest with energy and persistence before the local authorities against every
                    kind of repairs and succor for the corsair, as contrary to the royal decree of
                    June 17, 1861, and offensive to the government of the United States, with which
                    Spain is at peace.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>PERRY, <hi rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
